stateDiagram-v2
    %% Physical purge keeps app Source claim, Ticket receipt and resolution dependencies.
    %% CURRENT implementation; sources and guards in transition inventory.
    state "pending (status_id 10)" as pending
    state "authenticated (status_id 20)" as authenticated
    state "consumed (status_id 30)" as consumed
    state "canceled (status_id 90)" as canceled
    [*] --> pending
    pending --> authenticated: register_authentication!
    authenticated --> authenticated: prepare_result_delivery!
    authenticated --> consumed: consume!
    authenticated --> consumed: finalize_base! success
    consumed --> consumed: claim_authorization_grant!
    pending --> canceled: issue_cancellation! / cancel!
    authenticated --> canceled: issue_cancellation! before finalization
    canceled --> canceled: same-handoff delivery replay
    canceled --> [*]
    consumed --> [*]
    note right of pending
        Auth proof returns through opaque result to Base finalization.
        Visa result GET validates and displays a same-origin POST continuation only;
        authenticated finalization and code issuance occur on that protected POST.
        Consumed authorization can still claim its grant once for RP exchange.
        TTL refusal does not write an expired state.
        Cancellation handoff binding and cancel! commit under the parent lock in one Ticket transaction.
        Visa continuation delivers access_denied after this durable transition; it does not reserve the parent.
        A canceled parent refuses later results and finalization.
    end note
